 closely clipped nape and a scattering of freckles across the bridge of the nose. Usually dressed in a brown corduroy jacket with a narrow brass watch set a little fast, Darcy squares up pieces of paper while thinking when listening.","personality":"Darcy thinks best while walking. Sitting beneath someone's office clock makes Darcy sound more certain than they feel, an effect close friends have learned to distrust.","agenda":"To enter the shortlist under the chosen name.","family":"Rowan Kelly is Darcy’s older cousin. Darcy puts the kettle on. Rowan chooses the music. The cups come out before either brings up the reason for the visit. They trust a difficult conversation more if it has had an ordinary beginning. Asked about *Winter afloat*, Rowan says, “I budgeted for timber and forgot the cost of a bed.”","connections":"Cory Walker. One former applicant's embarrassment helps a new candidate choose a preferred name.","familyIds":["AH-R0891"],"connectionIds":["AH-R0624"],"reactions":[{"situation":"The founder is asked to use a formal name","response":"Darcy leaves the founder to decide what her own name on a letter should be.","asWritten":"The founder is asked to use a formal name. Darcy leaves the founder to decide what her own name on a letter should be."},{"situation":"A neighbor offers to pay for a favor that was meant kindly","response":"Darcy asks for help with a task the neighbor does well, so both people get to contribute something.","asWritten":"A neighbor offers to pay for a favor that was meant kindly. Darcy asks for help with a task the neighbor does well, so both people get to contribute something."},{"situation":"When family demands an immediate answer","response":"Darcy asks them to walk to the corner together and listen until the corner comes.","asWritten":"When family demands an immediate answer, Darcy asks them to walk to the corner together and listen until the corner comes."}]},"appearanceSource":"biography casting design"}},{"mesh":6,"name":"Hair_